WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.414
Secure IoT device design is a set of
repeatable habits.

2
00:00:03.494 --> 00:00:07.676
Start by defining trust boundaries across
device components, network paths,

3
00:00:07.756 --> 00:00:12.000
local interfaces, physical access, stored
state, identity, privileged code,

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.474
and cloud communication.

5
00:00:13.554 --> 00:00:17.102
When the boundaries are visible, design
review becomes concrete.

6
00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:19.209
Validate input and protect identity.

7
00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:21.507
Which interfaces accept external input?

8
00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.360
How is malformed input rejected?

9
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.088
Where are credentials stored?

10
00:00:25.168 --> 00:00:26.878
What code may use keys or tokens?

11
00:00:26.958 --> 00:00:28.859
What network services are exposed?

12
00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:32.550
These questions should have clear answers
in code, configuration,

13
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.150
and release documentation.

14
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.814
Keep C behavior predictable.

15
00:00:35.894 --> 00:00:40.076
Review fixed buffers, stack limits, heap
policy, memory pools, parser state,

16
00:00:40.156 --> 00:00:42.943
integer sizes, object lifetime, and
cleanup paths.

17
00:00:43.023 --> 00:00:47.521
A connected device is easier to secure
when memory and state transitions are bounded

18
00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:49.629
under normal and unusual conditions.

19
00:00:49.709 --> 00:00:52.053
Harden production builds and update flows.

20
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.730
Which debug or factory features remain
enabled?

21
00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.711
How is startup integrity verified?

22
00:00:56.791 --> 00:01:00.212
How are updates authorized, staged, rolled
back, or recovered?

23
00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:04.790
What happens if configuration is missing
or a reset happens at an inconvenient time?

24
00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.707
Finally, test failure, recovery,

25
00:01:06.787 --> 00:01:10.018
and diagnostic behavior under realistic
field conditions.

26
00:01:10.098 --> 00:01:13.836
Exercise credential errors, malformed
messages, network timeouts,

27
00:01:13.916 --> 00:01:18.224
reset behavior, update failure, full
storage, production versus debug builds,

28
00:01:18.304 --> 00:01:19.825
and privacy-aware logging.

29
00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:22.376
Secure IoT products are maintained over
time,

30
00:01:22.456 --> 00:01:25.940
so the design must support operations as
well as initial release.
